WEBVTT

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.280
So this was the hideout of Alit and others?

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:05.480
Yeah.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.400
Those guys haven't appeared once since then.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.340
Could it be they fled from this world?

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.910
Detective Yuma, please be careful of your choice of words.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.330
Because I am the officer and you are my subordinate.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.540
Se... Seriously?

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.000
On the other hand, depending on how hard you work, you might get a Rank-Up along with this.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.140
This is a Barian Police Identification card.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.910
Whoa! How cool!

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.250
By the way, how is Astral?

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.450
Oh, right...

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.220
Since the Duel with Gilag, he hasn't come out.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.640
I wonder if his body hasn't recovered yet?

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.170
Is that so...? You should know this by now,

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.370
that my business should be kept secret even from Astral.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.620
But about that... I don't like keeping secrets...

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:59.170
All this is for Astral's sake, too, Detective Yuma.

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:02.410
Roger! Understood, Officer Shingetsu!

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:07.940
<i>The powerful Monsters that the Barians used,
the Over Hundred Numbers...</i>

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:11.850
<i>Additionally, they evolve into Chaos Numbers.</i>

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.650
<i>With our power right now, there is no guarantee that we can win next time.</i>

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.370
<i>What should we do?</i>

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.400
Just what... is happening?

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:26.250
The Numbers?

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.510
Are they are trying to tell me something?

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.140
Astral.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.370
You're... Number 96!

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:40.820
Things seem to be going horrible with those Barian guys, huh?

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:43.880
Why? Your power should have been sealed!

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:47.650
True... But that doesn't mean I will obey you.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:48.800
How's this...?

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:53.250
Rather than putting my hands in my lap, I'll lend you my power?

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:56.370
I wouldn't borrow power from someone like you.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.650
As you like. Let me tell you something nice.

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:04.450
You haven't recovered the true memory of your Numbers yet.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:08.910
You should try to listen again. To us Numbers, that is.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:13.650
Astral, if you're the light, I am the darkness.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.650
Where there is light, there's always darkness.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:22.310
<i>That's right, absolutely right, and then...</i>

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.510
Astral... Astral....

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:26.910
<i>Then let's take a look at the next problem. First, this one...</i>

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.770
Astral... Hey, Astral!

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.820
Hey, Yuma, what are you doing?

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.910
He just won't come out, so...

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:38.250
Oh right! Teach! Can I go to the infirmary?!

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.420
I've gathered 50 of the Numbers so far...

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:46.570
Within these, there are memories I still haven't recovered...?

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:50.910
What is...?

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.020
This place...!

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.420
I am the one who shall test thee.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.220
Test... me...?

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.710
To obtain the memory of the Numbers.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.400
Everything will begin to move from that point.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:14.050
The memory of the Numbers?

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:17.420
Now is...!?

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.770
Thi... this person is...?!

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:29.420
I am the one who shall test thee.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.770
We shall Duel thee.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.500
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:44.470
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:47.180
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.530
<i>Preparations for the fight are ready</i>

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.610
<i>I can already hear the shivering of my heart</i>

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:07.120
<i>Been waiting this whole time</i>

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.490
<i>I may meet with defeat...</i>

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.710
<i>But that's exactly why I have to stand back up</i>

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:17.250
<i>Need to get stronger again</i>

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.380
<i>It's good to believe</i>

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:22.090
<i>The "now", more than ever before, is</i>

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.550
<i>but another limit to break down</i>

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:27.600
<i>I can cross with ease</i>

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:30.060
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:36.100
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.860
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.320
<i>Right here in my hand,</i>

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:45.030
<i>I'm holding a powerful trump card.</i>

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:54.080
<i>With an unbreakable heart, I face toward my dream!</i>

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.410
Astral...

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.830
Wait, Yuma-<i>kun</i>...

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:10.370
What are you doing there?

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:15.120
"Fighting Together with Dark Astral:
The Challenge Towards the Giant of Shadows!!"

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:15.410
You see... Astral hasn't come out of the key at all!

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.000
He must be sick!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.750
But that's...

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.050
Hey, Astral! You all right?

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:24.800
I'll get you some medicine right away!

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.180
Like I said...!

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.010
Oh, Kotori-<i>san</i>, calm down.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:31.430
Wha... What the?!

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:38.810
Oh...

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:43.780
Huh? Yuma is...?! Yuma's gone!

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:48.870
Thi... this is...

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.500
Th-This place...!

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.130
A... Astral!

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.170
This means...we're inside the Emperor's Key?

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.090
That's right.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.550
Why am I...?

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:12.140
He probably called you here.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:14.270
Who... who is that guy?

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:15.390
I don't know.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:19.270
While I was absorbing the memories of the Numbers, he suddenly appeared.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.310
Is this guy a Barian?

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:22.570
No, he's not.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:26.190
But it seems unavoidable that we Duel him.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:29.700
I am the one who shall test thee!

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:34.040
I don't have a clue what's going on, but let's do this!

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.830
Duel Disk, set!

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:42.920
D-Gazer, set!

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:44.750
Duel!!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:49.630
Through suffering, thou shall get stronger or be crushed!

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.850
My turn! Draw!

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.350
I Summon Bubble Blader!

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:04.070
Then, when a Bubble Blader is sent from my hand to the Graveyard,

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:08.990
I can Special Summon one more Bubble Blader from my hand.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.320
Resurrection of the Dead, activate!

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.990
The Bubble Blader from the Graveyard is Special Summoned.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.160
Three Monsters all at once!

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:24.210
I Overlay the three Level Four Bubble Bladers.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:28.710
I use these three Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.800
Xyz Summon!

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:38.520
Unformed Void the Fictitious King!

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:40.640
Zero Attack Points?

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:42.650
He's up to something. Be careful!

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:46.110
The Field Magic, Overlay World, activates.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:50.070
At the end of each turn, those without Xyz Monsters

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.240
receive 500 points damage.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.830
And destroyed Xyz Monsters are banished!

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.040
I end my turn.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.660
It's a card tied to Xyz Monsters!

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:03.670
Yuma, this is bad!

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:13.970
Effect Damage straight away...

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:18.180
Like hell I'll lose!
My turn! Draw!

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.640
Yuma, let's go full power!

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.480
Yeah! I Summon Dododo Warrior!

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.690
By lowering this Monster's Attack Power by 500 points,

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.860
it can be Summoned without release.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.900
Then the Magic Card, Forcing activates!

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.280
By sending one card from my hand to the Graveyard,

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:39.830
one Spellcaster-Type Monster 
can be Special Summoned from the hand.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.870
I'm sending Ganbalancer to the Graveyard

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.000
to Special Summon Gagaga Magician!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:51.300
Then the Magic Card, Resurrection of the Dead, activates!

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:54.840
I revive this guy from the Graveyard.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.340
Come, Ganbalancer!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:02.600
Ganbalancer can be treated as two units 
when used for an Xyz Summon!

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:07.610
Right! I Overlay the Ganbalancer counting as two!

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:11.570
With this double Monster I build the Overlay Network!

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:13.490
Xyz Summon!

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:19.830
Come forth, Number 61! Volcosaurus!

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:29.670
Good, Yuma! Summon one more Number!

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.210
Alright! Gagaga Magician's effect activates!

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.510
I change his level from four to six!

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:40.550
I Overlay the Level Six Dododo Warrior and Gagaga Magician!

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.680
Xyz Summon!

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:47.060
Appear, Number 6!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.780
OOParts Atlantal!

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.450
This mass deployment's fantastic!

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.250
Yuma, let's finish him straight off!

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:08.040
Right! I activate Atlantal's effect!

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.630
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.840
I can halve the opponent's Life Points once per turn!

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:18.510
Go, Atlantal! Orichalcum Gate!

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:27.430
Great! That guy's got some huge damage!

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:30.100
Then I can attack with our Numbers after that!

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.940
The effect of Unformed Void activates.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:38.360
By detaching one Overlay Unit once per turn during the opponent's turn,

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:42.070
The total Attack Power of the opponent's Xyz Monsters

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:45.660
is added to this Monster's Attack Power.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.350
5100 Attack Points!

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:13.480
The Attack Power of our Monsters was...

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:15.190
What's with that guy?!

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:18.280
But this Duel will be ours soon!

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:21.200
Volcosaurus' effect activates!

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:25.450
I can detach one Overlay Unit to destroy one Monster the opponent controls,

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:28.000
and its Attack Power will be inflicted as damage!

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:29.830
Mag-Max!

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.290
This is the end!

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:33.420
No...

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.380
Why... why wasn't that guy's Monster destroyed?

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.180
The Field Magic, Overlay World...

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:47.600
Both our Xyz Monsters can't be destroyed by Spells, Traps, or Monster Effects.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:52.060
Such an effect... I'll end my turn with this.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.770
My turn! Draw!

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:58.320
Unformed Void attacks Atlantal.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:01.740
Because Atlantal is a Number, it can't be destroyed!

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.030
That's right!

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:08.950
When Unformed Void attacks, effects that prevent destruction are negated.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:09.750
Impossible!

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.460
That means Atlantal is...

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:29.770
Damn! That guy is terribly strong!

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:32.020
In order to defeat this Monster...

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.780
Doesn't that seem to be quite interesting?

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:42.150
Yuma... Astral.

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:46.570
Number 96! How come this guy's...?!

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.120
Astral, that opponent...

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:54.250
seems to be there to test your worthiness as a Numbers User Duelist.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.080
Say what?

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:56.710
Testing Astral?

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:00.170
Why is a guy like that...?

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:03.420
Astral, you realized, didn't you?

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.890
Without my power, you won't be able to defeat this guy.

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.720
No way! Is that true?

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:13.560
Without me, you won't have enough power.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:18.650
The malice, the hate, the anger! You don't have a heart of evil!

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:22.280
Stop joking! Why would someone need that?

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:23.940
Beats me!

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:32.330
Astral, if you release me, I'm fine lending you my strength.

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:34.750
This isn't the human world.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:39.790
If you lose, I wonder what will become of Yuma...

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:44.380
Astral, don't listen! You don't want to have an evil heart!

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:47.970
My turn! Draw!

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.600
I set a Monster in Face-Down Defense Position!

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:55.140
Then I change Volcosaurus into Defense Position.

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:00.020
Unformed Void's effect activates.

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:02.730
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:06.650
the total Attack Power of the Xyz Monsters on the opponent's field

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.200
is added to this Monster's!

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:14.910
That effect again?

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:24.300
7600 Attack Points!?

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.260
Yuma, set the card!

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.430
I set one card and end my turn!

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.510
My turn! Draw!

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:36.480
Unformed Void attacks Volcosaurus!

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:38.770
That's bad!

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:53.280
I end my turn with this.

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:57.870
With our Xyz Monster gone, we'll get hit again by the...

00:14:57.870 --> 00:14:59.080
Field Magic's effect!

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.970
<i>Next time will be the last turn we have left.</i>

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.850
<i>If we can't Summon an Xyz Monster,</i>

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:20.600
<i>our Life will run out due to the Field Magic's effect.</i>

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.900
<i>But if we Summon an Xyz Monster,</i>

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.690
<i>we'll lose if it goes on like this!</i>

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:31.910
Sh... shoot.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:35.160
<i>If you lose...</i>

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:38.540
<i>I wonder what will become of Yuma...</i>

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.080
<i>Yuma...</i>

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:47.880
All right! Number 96, you're released!

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:51.720
What?! Hey, Astral... You...

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:55.720
Number 96, let me receive your power!

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.770
You idiot! Why use the power of a guy like him?!

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:12.570
As promised, I'll let you guys win.

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:16.070
Now, Summon my other self, Yuma!

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:17.740
Ba... bastard!

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:18.370
Yuma!

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.330
Right now, we have to win the Duel!

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.170
My turn...

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:28.800
Draw!

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:32.300
I Flip Summon the set Monster on my field.

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:35.430
Come, Magical Undertaker!

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:40.680
Then I activate Magical Undertaker's Flip Effect!

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:46.100
I Special Summon one Level Four or lower
Spellcaster-Type Monster from my Graveyard!

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:49.320
Be revived, Gagaga Magician!

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:53.030
Then, when I have a Dark-Attribute Monster on my field,

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.780
I can Special Summon this guy from my hand!

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:58.200
Come, Kurokurokuro!

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:01.830
Gagaga Magician's effect activates!

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:04.330
His level is changed from four to two!

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:08.840
You can do it if you really try, Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:10.250
Yuma!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:11.130
I know!

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:17.970
I Overlay the Level Two Magigal Undertaker, Kurokurokuro, and Gagaga Magician!

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:23.390
With these three Monsters, I build the Overlay Network!

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.350
Xyz Summon!

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:29.400
Come forth, Number 96!

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.450
Black Mist!

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.490
The headliner's appeared!

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:44.540
Come on and crush everything!

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:48.000
Black Mist, attack Unformed Void!

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:53.130
This moment, Black Mist's effect activates!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.470
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:59.220
the Attack Power of one opposing Monster is halved,

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:03.180
and this monster's Attack Power is increased by that amount!

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:05.230
Shadow Gain!

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:12.230
Now, Yuma! The Trap Card!

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:12.980
Right...

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.570
Trap, activate! Battle Restart!

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:20.120
This card returns a battle already started to its beginning, so it can start again.

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:24.290
At this moment, I activate Black Mist's effect again!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:26.620
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:29.250
the Attack Power of the opponent's Monster is halved,

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.250
and added to this Monster's!

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.090
Shadow Gain!

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:41.850
With this, that guy will be shred to bits!

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:43.970
Did you understand, Astral?

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:46.680
You <i>need</i> my power!

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:48.980
The power of <i>evil</i>, that is...

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:54.690
Now, go, Black Mist! Attack Unformed Void!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.690
Black Mirage Whip!

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:27.140
This... is from my dreams!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:31.900
Remember it, Astral. Your mission.

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:36.610
Wha... what is this?

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:42.030
Perhaps the door is showing me the path to my memory.

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:46.080
My true memories are in front of us.

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:47.740
True memories?

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.750
I see, so that's how it was...

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.050
I'm remembering it, Yuma.

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:03.970
This is the card that documents everything about the world.

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:08.140
Inside this card is how the world developed,

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:10.560
and where it is heading to.

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:13.980
Its past and its future... all is written in there.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.650
Wa... wait a sec. Just what does this mean?

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:22.530
This card is the fate of all the world, the power that decides everything.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.570
You may believe it or not,

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:28.620
but the world was born from just this one card.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.910
The God Card that created the entire world.

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:34.290
It's a Numeron Code.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:36.250
Numeron Code?

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:42.550
The Numbers I'm yet to collect hold its location.

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:47.680
My mission is to find this card before the Barians do.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:52.270
A... again?!

00:20:58.400 --> 00:20:59.110
Kotori!

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:00.860
Yuma!

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.030
You're back safe!

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:05.200
Astral!

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:09.450
Wha... what is this?

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.710
As we agreed, I will now remain released.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.170
Keep this in mind, Astral.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:22.630
You'll be needing the power of evil for the future that you're about to face.

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:29.350
What just happened right now?

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:36.060
You mean you had a Duel inside the Emperor's Key?

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:37.150
Yeah.

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:40.150
That thing earlier was Number 96.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:43.940
He ran away from the spaceship inside the Emperor's Key.

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:49.370
And I saw the Numeron Code inside Astral's memories.

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:54.370
Numeron Code? Just what is that...?

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:58.670
<i>The words Number 96 said...</i>

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:02.800
<i>That I'll need evil for the coming future...</i>

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:07.930
<i>Will I really...need something like that?</i>

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:24.480
<i>Does the thought "In any case..." following</i>

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:32.160
<i>the foreboding premonition tell you to give up?</i>

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:39.750
<i>Do you laugh at your dreams, saying "impossible"?</i>

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:47.090
<i>You must find it funny that I'm not able to laugh at it, right?</i>

00:22:47.630 --> 00:23:04.020
<i>This song supports me, so I'll do my best for you this time.
 It's my turn to sing now.</i>

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:08.820
<i>I will vow to you here</i>

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:19.160
<i>As long as I live, you'll always be my tiny, little friend</i>

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:27.710
<i>I'll erase all those little mistakes of yours</i>

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:32.510
<i>Because I want to become an artist</i>

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:38.810
<i>Look, I like doing it 'cuz it's fun.</i>

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:43.520
I've received a letter of challenge.

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:46.780
And the sender was... Orbital 7?!

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:49.860
And he wants to Duel me with Obomi at stake?

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:52.660
Orbital, could you possibly have a thing for Obomi-<i>chan</i>?

00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:55.160
What exactly...am I supposed to do?

00:23:55.280 --> 00:23:57.990
Show me the tactics similar to Kaito.

00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:00.620
Activate now, Djinn Orchestra!

00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:02.830
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:02.830 --> 00:24:06.460
"Operation: Save Obomi!?
 I, a Lover, am Invincible!"

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:09.090
This is... Galaxy Eyes?
